insert into kb_articles (slug, title, body_md, category, tags, is_published) values
  ($kbf$help-reviews$kbf$, $kbf$Customer reviews + Google link$kbf$, $kbf$Reviews shown on the public site are curated manually — you decide
what appears. Manage them at `/admin/reviews`.

How it works:

- Copy the text of a review from Google/Facebook/Yelp/email

- In `/admin/reviews` click **Add review** → paste it, set name, rating, source, optional photo + date

- Toggle **Featured** to put it in the homepage carousel (limit 3 visible at a time, they auto-rotate every 7s)

- Toggle **Visible** off to hide without deleting

Where they show up:

- **Homepage carousel** above the trust strip — only "Featured + Active" ones, max 12 in rotation

- **/reviews page** — ALL active reviews, sorted Featured first, then most recent

- Linked from the public header (Info → Reviews)

💡 The **"Leave us a Google review"** CTA on both pages
uses the `google_review_url` setting (default points to
your maps.app.goo.gl link). Edit it in `/admin/site`
under the "reviews" category if your Google place ID changes.

💡 Phase 2 idea: auto-sync from Google Places API so new reviews
appear without manual copy-paste. Requires Google Cloud project +
API key + billing. Ask when you want to set this up.$kbf$, $kbf$Customer$kbf$, array[$kbf$help$kbf$, $kbf$imported$kbf$], true)
