insert into kb_articles (slug, title, body_md, category, tags, is_published) values
  ($kbf$help-coi$kbf$, $kbf$Certificates of Insurance (COI) for venues$kbf$, $kbf$Many venues (schools, parks, churches, HOAs, corporate offices)
require proof of insurance with them listed as additional insured
before they let you set up bounce houses on their property.

How the flow works:

- At checkout, customer checks **"My venue requires a Certificate of Insurance"**

- They fill venue name, address, who to list as additional insured, any special instructions

- On booking creation, a row is added to `coi_requests` with status **requested**

- You see the request in `/admin/coi` with all the venue details

- You call/email your insurance broker → they generate the COI PDF

- Back in `/admin/coi`, click **Upload COI**, attach the PDF

- Customer gets emailed automatically + the COI shows on their `/portal/bookings/[id]` page with a download button

- Optionally click **Mark delivered to venue** after you've sent it directly to the venue contact

Where to manage:

- `/admin/coi` — pending requests panel with upload

- Each booking detail page links to its COI request

- Disable the checkbox at checkout with the green/grey toggle at the top of `/admin/coi` (mirrors the Packages + Gift cards toggles)

💡 The PDF lives in your public Supabase storage (site-assets bucket).
That's fine — COIs aren't sensitive (they just name your insurance
carrier + policy number).$kbf$, $kbf$Policies$kbf$, array[$kbf$help$kbf$, $kbf$imported$kbf$], true)
