insert into kb_articles (slug, title, body_md, category, tags, is_published) values
  ($kbf$help-unit-tracking$kbf$, $kbf$Per-unit asset tracking (which BLW-05 went where?)$kbf$, $kbf$For valuable items where you need to know *which physical unit*
was on which truck (blowers, generators, large bouncers), you can
tag each unit individually (BLW-01, BLW-02, ...) and assign specific
units to a route from dispatch.

One-time setup:

- Go to `Inventory` → click the item (e.g. "Blowers")

- Click **Enable unit tracking**

- Click **Bulk add (auto-tag)** → prefix `BLW`, count `14` → creates BLW-01 through BLW-14 instantly

- Optionally edit each unit to add serial number, acquired date, notes ("cracked housing", etc.)

- Physically label each unit with a sharpie / sticker matching its tag

Daily flow (per dispatch):

- Open `/admin/dispatch/[date]` → planned routes show the Truck Load section

- For each item that tracks units, you'll see "no units picked" + a **Pick units** button

- Click → modal lists every active unit with status dot (good / needs_repair / broken)

- Pick the specific units going on that truck → save

- The truck load card now shows tags like `BLW-03 BLW-07 BLW-11` instead of just "3× Blowers"

- Units assigned to another route on a different day are flagged red so you can't double-book

When a unit comes back damaged:

- Go to `Inventory` → item → find the unit → click pencil to edit

- Change condition to `needs_repair` or `broken`, add a note

- The status dot in dispatch dropdown will now show amber/red so you don't accidentally assign it again

💡 Don't enable unit tracking for high-volume consumables (sandbags,
cables, tarps). The overhead of picking specific units per route
isn't worth it. Reserve it for items you'd legitimately want to
trace ("which generator was at the Mendez delivery when it broke?").

💡 Phase 2 idea: driver scans QR codes printed on each unit to
confirm loading/return. Worth doing once you have 30+ tracked
units and crew rotation issues. Ask when ready.$kbf$, $kbf$Setup$kbf$, array[$kbf$help$kbf$, $kbf$imported$kbf$], true)
