  ($kbf$help-customer-tracking$kbf$, $kbf$Customer tracking page (Domino's-style timeline)$kbf$, $kbf$Every customer booking detail page at `/portal/bookings/[id]`
now shows a 6-step visual timeline that updates in real time as the
booking moves through its lifecycle. No more "where's my rental?"
phone calls.

The 6 steps:

- ✅ **Payment confirmed** — green check once Stripe clears

- ⏳ **X days until your event** — countdown with context-aware copy ("we'll send a reminder 3 days before" / "your event is tomorrow!")

- 📦 **Loaded on the truck** — activates when admin marks the route as `loaded` in /admin/dispatch. Shows driver + vehicle name.

- 🚚 **Driver on the way** — activates when route status is `out_for_delivery`

- ✨ **Delivered & set up** — when delivery stop is marked completed

- 📅 **Picked up** — when the pickup route is completed

The active step pulses with a yellow ring; done steps are green
with strikethrough. Special states handled: cancelled bookings
short-circuit to a single "Cancelled" card; weather cancellations
show the credit message.

💡 To make the timeline progress through "loaded" and "out for
delivery", you (admin) need to update the `dispatch_routes.status`
field as the day goes on — in `/admin/dispatch/[date]` there
should be a status dropdown per route.$kbf$, $kbf$Customer$kbf$, array[$kbf$help$kbf$, $kbf$imported$kbf$], true)
