insert into kb_articles (slug, title, body_md, category, tags, is_published) values
  ($kbf$help-quote-followup$kbf$, $kbf$Quote follow-up reminder (auto)$kbf$, $kbf$Quotes sent but not accepted often sit in a customer's inbox and
get forgotten. A daily cron at 4 PM EST finds quotes that are
**3+ days old, still in 'sent' or 'viewed' status, not
expired** — and emails a friendly reminder with a big
"View and Accept" button.

Logic:

- Runs daily at 16:00 UTC (cron in vercel.json)

- Only sends ONE reminder per quote (followup_sent_at marks it)

- Skips paid, declined, or expired quotes

- Up to 50 reminders per run (cap to avoid bursts)

- Email tagged as `quote_followup` for analytics

💡 To trigger manually for testing:
`curl -H "Authorization: Bearer $CRON_SECRET" https://itsalwaysfun-rental.vercel.app/api/cron/quote-followup`$kbf$, $kbf$Setup$kbf$, array[$kbf$help$kbf$, $kbf$imported$kbf$], true)
