insert into kb_articles (slug, title, body_md, category, tags, is_published) values
  ($kbf$help-1099-nec$kbf$, $kbf$1099-NEC year-end report (contractor tax filing)$kbf$, $kbf$The IRS requires a 1099-NEC for every non-employee paid
**$600 or more** in a calendar year. This page does the
compilation work for you so January doesn't become a scramble.

Where to find it:

`/admin/reports/1099-nec` — also reachable via the green
"1099-NEC year-end →" button on `/admin/reports`.

How it works:

- Sums every booking expense where the category has the
**supports_payroll_hours** flag (payroll, setup_labor,
teardown_labor, or any custom labor category) — grouped by
`driver_email` — for the selected calendar year

- Each row shows: total paid, hours, bookings, W9 status, TIN last 4,
address completeness, filed status

- Qualifying drivers (≥ threshold) are shown first; non-qualifying
ones below for reference

- The 5-stat header tracks: drivers w/ payments, qualifying count,
total paid out, missing W9 count, filed progress

January workflow:

- Switch to the closing tax year (year selector at top)

- For each qualifying driver missing W9, name, TIN, or address:
click **Profile** to fill it in, click **W9**
to mark received

- Download CSV → upload to your filing service (Track1099,
eFile4Biz, or hand to accountant)

- After each filing, click **Mark filed** so you can
track progress at a glance

- IRS deadline: **January 31** for both recipient copy +
IRS filing

💡 **TIN storage:** only the last 4 digits are stored in
the DB (for verification). The full SSN/EIN lives in the W9 PDF in
private Supabase storage (bucket: `w9`). Never paste a
full SSN into the notes field.

💡 The $600 threshold is configurable in
`site_settings.1099_nec_threshold_cents` — change it if
the IRS raises the limit.

⚙️ **Setup required (one time):** run
`supabase/driver_1099.sql`. Creates the
`driver_tax_profiles` table and seeds the threshold
site setting.$kbf$, $kbf$Billing$kbf$, array[$kbf$help$kbf$, $kbf$imported$kbf$], true)
